ARSDR1</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">14q23.3</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">0.0162936</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2.113388456</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">37999&#x0005f;at</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">CPO</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">3q12</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">0.028280124</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2.100322069</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">35978&#x0005f;at</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">PRRG1</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Xp21.1</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">0.028280124</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2.05552932</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">121&#x0005f;at</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">PAX8</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">2q12-q14</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">0.028280124</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2.028946437</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">41715&#x0005f;at</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">PIK3C2B</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">1q32</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">0.00902344</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2.024856688</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">41644&#x0005f;at</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">KIAA0790</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">6q24.3</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">0.047201768</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2.004743183</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap>). Included in this group of genes are <italic>epidermal growth factor type 2 receptor (c-erbB2), inhibin (INHBB), multiple endocrine neoplasia I (MEN1), growth factor receptor-bound protein 7 (GRB7), BCL2, E-cadherin (CDH1)</italic> and <italic>syndecan (SDC2)</italic> (<xref rid="tbl3" ref-type="table">Table 3</xref>). Importantly, <italic>c-erbB2</italic> gene was the most highly differentially expressed gene in USPC when compared to OSPC (<xref rid="tbl3" ref-type="table">Table 3</xref>, <xref rid="tbl4" ref-type="table">Table 4</xref><table-wrap id="tbl4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Differentially expressed genes in USPC and OSPC ranked by significance analysis of microarrays (SAM)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Order</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Probeset</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Gene ID</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Score (<italic>d</italic>)</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Numerator (<italic>r</italic>)</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Denominator (<italic>s</italic>&#x0002b;<italic>s</italic>0)</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Fold change</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold><italic>q</italic>-value (&#x00025;)</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02002;1</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">39470&#x0005f;at</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">39470&#x0005f;at</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2.5193455</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">3.596293949</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">1